  "strategy": "We are to minimize the auto-convolution peak-to-root-mean-square (PRMS) ratio: `2*n*max_convolution / sum_a^2`, where `sum_a` is the sum of coefficients after clipping.\nThe best candidate length is 768, as previously found. We will use a two-phase optimization: \n1. Preconditioning with a shifted log-sum-exp of the convolution indices.\n2. Normalized coordinate descent to further reduce peaks.\n\nWe need to define:\n1. A global optimization method for the original length.\n2. A fallback if time is short.\n\nThe core challenge is the lack of Lipschitz continuity when using `np.dot` on large arrays, so we use FFT-based convolution with dual boundaries.\n\nWe'll implement:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom scipy.stats import truncnorm\nfrom scipy.fft import rfft, irfft\n\ndef evaluate_sequence(seq):\n    \"\"\"Original evaluator, cannot change.\"\"\"\n    # The implementation is given but we'll use it directly.\n\nclass LogSumExpConv:\n    \"\"\"Optimization specific to auto-convolution.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n_const, T_initial=1000.0, T_final=1.0, n_steps=6000):\n        self.n_const = n_const\n        self.T_initial = T_initial\n        self.n_steps = n_steps\n\n    def _obj(self, z):\n        # Objective function for L-BFGS-B\n        a = softmax(z)\n        conv_fft = irfft(rfft(a)**2)[1:-1]  # Pruning the convolution to exclude edges\n        max_conv = np.log(np.sum(np.exp(conv_fft * self.T_initial)) / n_step\n        # ... complete the obj function\n\n    def _start_from_parent(self):\n        # Use the parent sequence if available, normalize it.\n        parent = height_sequence_1\n        # Smooth it and initialize factors\n\ndef simplex_coordinate_descent(a, n_steps=2500):\n    \"\"\"\n    Continuously projects onto the simplex-normalized log-space representation.\n    Input: sequence of coefficients (numpy array)\n    Output: improved sequence\n    \"\"\"\n    original_length = a.size\n    # Use logarithms and find averages\n\n    # Implement coordinate descent with projection at each change\n\n    # HundredTinyIrregularGraduations and clip to boundaries\n\ndef propose_candidate(parent=height_sequence_1, time_limit=1800):\n    # Backup parent sequence with dual boundaries applied.\n    n_initial = len(parent)\n    \n    def make_candidate_from_parent(b_factor=0.8, smooth=0.1):\n        candidate = parent * b_factor\n        candidate = candidate + smooth * np.random.randn(n_initial)\n        return candidate\n\n    # BP(optimizer sometimes encounters)\n\n    # Step 1: Try to exploit the parent's smoothness.\n    candidate = make_candidate_from_parent()\n    score1 = evaluate_sequence(candidate)\n    \n    # Step 2: If improvement, we do coordinate descent.\n    # We also do a short L-BFGS-B rounding and then simplex CD.\n\n    # Step 3: Fallback to the parent if no improvement.\n    best = parent.copy()\n    best_score = min(evaluate_sequence(parent), score1)\n\n    # Step 4: Run up to 1/3rd time in multi-phase CD, else use one phase.\n\n    # Execute (up to 3) combined smoothing refinements.\n\n    # Step 5: If we improve, return best sequence.\n\n    # Final result should be validated.\n\n    # Print intermediate results.\n\n    # Format and timing.",
